# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CONFIGURATION [Cc]
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# # Cc.1 Pattern Syntax [SYNTAX]
#
#   Purpose:  Configuration — how to read patterns
#   Contains: Pattern matching rules and conventions
#
# Syntax Rules:
#   - Blank lines are ignored
#   - Lines starting with # are comments
#   - ! negates a pattern (includes previously excluded)
#   - / at end means directory only
#   - * matches anything except /
#   - ** matches across directories

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPERATIONS [Co]
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# # Co.1 Build Artifacts [BUILD]
#
#   Purpose:  Generated files that shouldn't be tracked
#   Patterns: Compiled binaries, object files, build directories
#

# Compiled binaries
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.out

# Object files
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib

# Build directories
/build/
/dist/
/out/
/bin/
/target/

# [Project-specific build artifacts]
# [Add your build output directories here]

# # Co.2 Dependencies [DEPS]
#
#   Purpose:  External packages managed by package managers
#   Patterns: node_modules, vendor, venv, target
#

# Node.js
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Go
/vendor/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.Python
venv/
ENV/
.venv/

# Rust
/target/
Cargo.lock

# [Project-specific dependencies]
# [Add your dependency directories here]

# # Co.3 IDE and Editor [IDE]
#
#   Purpose:  Local configuration not shared across team
#   Patterns: .vscode, .idea, vim swap files, emacs temp
#

# VSCode (keep .vscode/settings.json if sharing project settings)
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# JetBrains IDEs
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr

# Vim
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.netrwhist

# Emacs
*~
\#*\#
/.emacs.desktop
/.emacs.desktop.lock
*.elc

# [Project-specific IDE files]
# [Add your IDE-specific ignores here]

# # Co.4 Environment and Secrets [SECRETS]
#
#   Purpose:  Credentials and sensitive configuration — NEVER commit these
#   Patterns: .env files, *.pem, *.key, credentials.json
#

# Environment files
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.development
.env.test
.env.production

# Credentials and keys
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.json

# API keys and tokens
.api-key
.token

# [Project-specific secrets]
# [Add patterns for any project-specific sensitive files]

# # Co.5 OS Generated [OS]
#
#   Purpose:  System files that vary by machine
#   Patterns: .DS_Store, Thumbs.db, .directory
#

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*

# Windows
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# Linux
*~
.directory

# # Co.6 Logs and Temporary [LOGS]
#
#   Purpose:  Generated logs, temp files, and test output
#   Patterns: *.log, *.tmp, coverage/, .cache/
#

# Logs
*.log
logs/
log/

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.backup
.cache/
tmp/
temp/

# Coverage and test results
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov
.coverage
htmlcov/

# # Co.7 Project-Specific [PROJECT]
#
#   Purpose:  Custom patterns unique to this project
#   Patterns: [Add project-specific patterns below]
#

# [Example: Ignore generated documentation]
# /docs/generated/

# [Example: Ignore local configuration overrides]
# *.local.yaml

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VERIFICATION [Cv]
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# # Cv.1 Validation [VALIDATION]
#
#   Purpose:  Verify gitignore is working correctly
#   Commands: git check-ignore, git status --ignored
#
# Verify Commands:
#   git check-ignore -v [filename]    # Check if file would be ignored
#   git status --ignored              # List all ignored files
#
# Common Issues:
#   - "File still tracked" → Already committed files need: git rm --cached [file]
#   - "Pattern not working" → Check for typos, trailing spaces
#   - "Too many files ignored" → Pattern may be too broad, use ! to negate

# # Cv.2 Security [SECURITY]
#
#   Purpose:  Credential protection and recovery guidance
#   Critical: .env, *.pem, *.key files MUST be ignored
#
# Gitignore protects secrets:
#   - .env files contain credentials - MUST be ignored
#   - *.pem, *.key files contain private keys
#   - credentials.json, secrets.yaml contain sensitive config
#
# If secrets were accidentally committed:
#   1. Rotate all exposed credentials immediately
#   2. Use BFG or git filter-repo to remove from history
#   3. Force push (coordinate with team)
#
# # Cv.3 Maintenance [MAINTENANCE]
#
#   Purpose:  Safe modification guidance for this configuration
#   Levels:   Safe / Careful / Never
#
# Safe to Modify:
#   ✅ Add new patterns for project-specific files
#   ✅ Add comments explaining patterns
#   ✅ Use ! to include specific files from ignored directories
#
# Modify with Care:
#   ⚠️ Removing patterns (may expose sensitive files)
#   ⚠️ Broad patterns like * or **/* (may exclude needed files)
#   ⚠️ Patterns affecting shared IDE configs
#
# NEVER Modify:
#   ❌ Remove .env and secrets patterns without team discussion
#   ❌ 3-block data structure

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# END CONTENT
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CLOSING [CLOSING]
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# 3-Block Data Structure: Operational guidance and closing notes
#
# Section order: Policy → Extension → Troubleshooting → Reference → Note → Template → Omission
# Flow: modify → extend → debug → lookup → ground → instantiate → reserve
#
# (Note: Validation/Security/Maintenance are in CONTENT as Cv.1-Cv.3)
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# # X.1 Policy [POLICY]
#
#   Purpose:  Guide future maintainers — what's safe to change
#   Contains: Safe / Careful / Never modification levels
#
# Safe to Modify:
#   ✅ Add new pattern categories (Co.*)
#   ✅ Add project-specific patterns
#   ✅ Add comments explaining patterns
#
# Modify with Care:
#   ⚠️ Removing patterns (may expose sensitive files)
#   ⚠️ Broad patterns like * or **/* (may exclude needed files)
#   ⚠️ Patterns affecting shared IDE configs
#
# NEVER Modify:
#   ❌ 3-block structure (METADATA, CONTENT, CLOSING)
#   ❌ Remove .env and secrets patterns without team discussion
#   ❌ Remove Cv.* verification sections
#
# Validation: See Cv.1 for verification commands.

# # X.2 Extension [EXTENSION]
#
#   Purpose:  How to expand this gitignore — mirrors M.10 Roadmap
#   Contains: Extension patterns, planned additions
#
# Adding New Pattern Categories:
#   1. Add Co.N section with schema and docstring
#   2. Add patterns organized by type
#   3. Add [Project-specific] placeholder
#
# Adding New Patterns:
#   1. Place in appropriate Co.* category
#   2. Add comment explaining purpose
#   3. Test with git check-ignore
#
# Architecture: See CONTENT for Cc/Co/Cv structure.
# Roadmap: See M.10 for planned pattern additions.

# # X.3 Troubleshooting [TROUBLESHOOTING]
#
#   Purpose:  Common problems and solutions — gitignore issues
#
# "File still being tracked":
#   → Already committed files need: git rm --cached [file]
#
# "Pattern not working":
#   → Check for typos, trailing spaces
#   → Verify pattern syntax in Cc.1
#
# "Too many files ignored":
#   → Pattern may be too broad, use ! to negate
#
# "Secrets exposed":
#   → See Cv.2 Security for recovery steps
#
# Pattern-specific troubleshooting in CONTENT Co.* section docstrings.

# # X.4 Reference [REFERENCE]
#
#   Purpose:  Quick lookup — copy-paste ready commands
#
# Verification:
#   git check-ignore -v [file]    # Check if file would be ignored
#   git status --ignored          # List all ignored files
#
# Recovery:
#   git rm --cached [file]        # Untrack already-committed file
#   git rm -r --cached .          # Untrack all, re-add fresh
#
# Debug:
#   git check-ignore -v *         # Check all files in current dir
#   cat .gitignore | grep -v '^#' # Show active patterns only

# # X.5 Closing Note [NOTE]
#
#   Purpose:  Final guidance and grounding — echoes M.8
#   Verse:    Ecclesiastes 3:6
#
# This gitignore defines repository boundaries — what belongs in version control
# and what should remain local or generated.
#
# "A time to keep, and a time to cast away." — Ecclesiastes 3:6
#
# May clear boundaries serve the project well.

# # X.6 Template Guidance [TEMPLATE]
#
#   Purpose:  How to use this template — remove when instantiating
#   Usage:    cp gitignore.gitignore .gitignore → update pragma → fill patterns
#
# Update on instantiation:
#   - M.1: Key, Title
#   - M.2: Created/Updated dates
#   - M.4: Path
#   - M.5: Derives_from (point to this template)
#   - M.9: Dependencies (if applicable)
#   - M.10: Roadmap (planned patterns)
#   - Co.*: Project-specific patterns
#
# Remove this section (X.6) when instantiating.

# # X.7 Omission Guide [OMISSION]
#
#   Purpose:  What can be reserved and why — guidance for CLOSING sections
#
#   All sections must be present. Empty sections use: [Reserved: reason]
#   Omit subsection content, never the subsection header itself.

